## 1. Introduction

### 1.1 Purpose

The purpose of this document is to outline the technical specifications required for the integration of automation systems, including industrial robots, sensors, and control systems, for manufacturing operations at Advanced Manufacturing Facility (AMF) located in Austin, TX. The document serves as a guideline for system design, development, and deployment to ensure efficiency and reliability.

### 1.2 Scope

The scope of this document encompasses the design, implementation, and operational requirements for the automation systems, particularly focusing on the integration of Fanuc M-20iA industrial robots, Omron sensors, and Siemens control systems. The automation project aims to enhance the production line efficiency by 30% within the next fiscal year.

### 1.3 Background

Advanced Automation Solutions, Inc. has been a leader in providing automation solutions for manufacturing since 2010. With over 100 successful projects, we aim to leverage our expertise in robotics and control systems to optimize AMF's operations.

### 1.4 Audience

This document is intended for project managers, engineers, technical staff, and stakeholders involved in the automation project at AMF. It is also a resource for compliance and safety teams.

