## 5. System Interfaces

### 5.1 Robot-to-Sensor Interfaces

- Communication between robots and sensors will utilize Ethernet/IP.
- Each robot will integrate with two proximity sensors and one vision sensor.

### 5.2 Control Systems Interfaces

- Siemens S7-1500 control systems will interface with both robots and sensors using Profinet.
- Data logging and monitoring will be facilitated through a centralized database managed by the IT team led by David Lee.

### 5.3 Human-Machine Interfaces (HMI)

- HMI systems will be designed by the engineering team, ensuring user-friendly navigation and clear visual displays.
- Training sessions will be held for operators to familiarize them with the HMI functionalities.

---

## 6. Testing and Validation

### 6.1 Testing Strategy

- **Component Testing:** Each component (robots, sensors, control systems) will be tested independently before integration.
- **Integration Testing:** After successful component testing, integration tests will be conducted to ensure all systems work together seamlessly.

### 6.2 Validation Process

- A validation report will be generated after testing, detailing the outcomes and any issues encountered.
- All issues must be resolved before the system is moved to the deployment stage.

